{number: 45}
{title: Jesus Paid It All}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] I hear the Savior say,
"Thy strength indeed is [G7] small;
Child of [C] weakness, watch and [F] pray,
Find in [C] Me thine [G7] all in [C] all."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Jesus paid it [Am] all,
[C] All to Him I [G] owe;
[C] Sin had left a [F] crimson stain,
He [C] washed it [G7] white as [C] snow.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Lord, now indeed I find
Thy pow'r, and Thine a-[G7] lone,
Can [C] change the leper's [F] spots
And [C] melt the [G7] heart of [C] stone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] For nothing good have I
Whereby Thy grace to [G7] claim;
I'll [C] wash my garments [F] white
In the [C] blood of [G7] Calv'ry's [C] Lamb.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
And [C] when before the throne
I stand in Him com-[G7] plete,
"Jesus [C] died my soul to [F] save,"
My [C] lips shall [G7] still re-[C] peat.
{end_of_verse}
